[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_agnes"
text = "# DRAFT
# Agnes, Hob's wife, by the fire in the Cross Keys, night 0. Motherly, and sharp.
# The bed answer gives him the room at the top (n0_room). An ale ends the talk; the next talk starts at again.
== start
(A woman by the fire with her sleeves rolled, stirring a pot. She looks you up and down.)
Agnes: Look at you, wet to the skin. Come by the fire before you catch your death.
-> topics

== again
-> again_room [if n0_room]
-> again_plain

== again_room
Agnes: Your room's made up, brother. Top of the stair, as far as it goes.
-> topics

== again_plain
Agnes: Well? Warmer?
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n0_room] Have you a bed for the night? -> bed
* [if not n0_agnes_abbey] What do you know of the abbey? -> abbey
* An ale, if you would. [drink] -> ale

== bed [set n0_room]
Agnes: A bed. There's the room at the top. It's small and it's cold, and its one window looks toward the abbey.
Agnes: Nobody else will have it. You can have it for a prayer and a ha'penny.
Agnes: Be in before the curfew bell at nine. After it the Keys is shut, and the street's no place to be.
-> topics

== abbey [set n0_agnes_abbey]
Agnes: I don't talk about that place under my own roof.
(She glances at the shutters all the same, and lowers her voice.)
Agnes: We've had lodgers go over there to see the relic. Paid me for two nights and slept one.
Agnes: I don't ask. I strip the bed and let it again.
-> topics

== ale
-> ale_more [if n0_agnes_poured]
-> ale_first

== ale_first [set n0_agnes_poured]
(She fills a cup from the jug and puts it into your hands.)
Agnes: Drink it slow. It's stronger than what your country brothers brew.
-> end

== ale_more
Agnes: Another? You'll be no use to your abbot in the morning.
(She fills it to the brim anyway.)
-> end

== leave
Agnes: Before nine, mind!
"
